the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is *an amount*.
    the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is *an amount*.
    the couple or living with spouse resource limit of *a person* is *an amount*.
    the individual no spouse resource limit of *a person* is *an amount*.

the knowledge base us_statutes_42_1382_a_3 includes:


% 42 U.S.C. 1382(a)(3) — us:statutes/42/1382/a/3
the text of "42 USC 1382(a)(3)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/3.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382(a)(3)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/3.yaml".

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is 2250 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1974-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1985-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is 2400 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1985-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1986-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is 2550 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1986-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1987-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is 2700 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1987-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1988-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is 2850 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1988-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1989-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is 3000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1989-01-01 <= D.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is 1500 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1974-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1985-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is 1600 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1985-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1986-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is 1700 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1986-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1987-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is 1800 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1987-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1988-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is 1900 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1988-01-01 <= D
    and D < 1989-01-01.

the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is 2000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 1989-01-01 <= D.

rule couple_or_living_with_spouse_resource_limit with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(3)(A)":
the couple or living with spouse resource limit of a person is an amount if
    the person is a person
    and the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is the amount.

rule individual_no_spouse_resource_limit with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(3)(B)":
the individual no spouse resource limit of a person is an amount if
    the person is a person
    and the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is the amount.

scenario resource_limits_prior_to_january_1985 is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/3.test.yaml" at case 1:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 1984-12-01.
    q_couple_or_living_with_spouse_resource_limit expects answers ["the couple or living with spouse resource limit of person_1 is 2250"].
    q_individual_no_spouse_resource_limit expects answers ["the individual no spouse resource limit of person_1 is 1500"].

scenario resource_limits_on_january_1985 is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/3.test.yaml" at case 2:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 1985-01-01.
    q_couple_or_living_with_spouse_resource_limit expects answers ["the couple or living with spouse resource limit of person_1 is 2400"].
    q_individual_no_spouse_resource_limit expects answers ["the individual no spouse resource limit of person_1 is 1600"].

scenario resource_limits_on_january_1989 is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/3.test.yaml" at case 3:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 1989-01-01.
    q_couple_or_living_with_spouse_resource_limit expects answers ["the couple or living with spouse resource limit of person_1 is 3000"].
    q_individual_no_spouse_resource_limit expects answers ["the individual no spouse resource limit of person_1 is 2000"].

